MODULE generating_array_OD
PURPOSE AFC extraction, station reconciliation, OD construction, compression, windows, and historical references.
PAPER Sections 3.2, 4.2.1-4.2.4; Equations (1)-(9); Section 4.3.2 Equation (15).

SCHEMA
    All software array indices are zero-based; station indices are 0..N-1.
    Retained destination slots are 0..R-1; residual slot is R in width K=R+1.
    Paper slot number k in 1..R maps to software slot k-1.
    station_order: immutable list of N canonical station identifiers.
    station_to_codes: canonical station index to distinct AFC station codes.
    code_to_station: AFC station code to one canonical station index.
    journey_id: stable identifier for deduplication; never published in output.
    entry_time: actual tap-in timestamp with declared timezone.
    exit_time: actual tap-out timestamp, possibly unresolved.
    entry_interval: interval containing entry_time under declared boundary rules.
    origin: canonical station known at entry.
    destination: canonical station observed at exit.
    count: passenger multiplicity; one for an individual journey.
    resolved_records: records whose eventual destination is known offline.
    observation_store: event-timed records accessible at a requested cutoff.
    actual_by_time[t]: full raw OD labels [N,N].
    label_completeness[t]: resolved-cohort status under the declared finalization policy.
    production_by_time[t]: entry-cohort row totals [N].
    attraction_by_time[t]: entry-cohort destination totals [N].
    exit_clock_counts: separate operational statistic if required; not substituted for attraction_by_time.
    split_manifest: train, validation, and test target-time membership.
    sample_manifest: forecast origins and explicit input/target timestamps.
    mapping_artifact: station order, RDS, residual sets, residual weights, fitting provenance.
    availability_manifest: when each source observation became accessible.
CONFIG
    Invalid-journey handling and label-finalization policy require declaration.
    Timezone, service-day rollover, interval closure, and boundary inclusion require declaration.
    Missing-period handling is distinct from an observed zero-demand period.
    The published study uses 15-minute intervals; other intervals are a changed task.
    The retained integer dimension must be supplied explicitly.
    No configuration value is inferred from an old filename.

PROCEDURE generate_OD_DO_array
    INPUT df: validated AFC journey or sufficient event-cohort records.
    INPUT x_y_time: ordered requested entry intervals.
    INPUT sz_conn_to_station_index: legacy name for station_to_codes.
    INPUT station_index_to_sz_conn: legacy name for code_to_station.
    INPUT base_dir, prefix: logical artifact destination and split identifier.
    INPUT station_manager_dict_file_path: station-order artifact.
    INPUT result_array_file_path: output artifact destination.
    INPUT contract: event-time schema, split manifest, label resolution policy.
    OUTPUT intermediate_dic: actual labels, independent totals, observation-store reference.
    REQUIRE prefix is one declared dataset split.
    REQUIRE output belongs to the intended dataset directory.
    READ station manager artifact.
    VERIFY canonical station indices are exactly 0..N-1 without gaps or duplicates.
    VERIFY graph and AFC maps use that same order.
    VALIDATE required event-time fields before grouping.
    IF only final OD counts with entry time are present:
        ALLOW construction of actual-demand labels.
        MARK real-time finished/unfinished construction unavailable.
    END IF
    REMOVE or flag duplicate journey records under the declared policy.
    RECONCILE AFC station codes with canonical station indices.
    IF an observed code has multiple canonical destinations:
        STOP with an ambiguous-mapping diagnostic.
    END IF
    GROUP resolved records by entry interval.
    PREPARE an empty mapping actual_by_time.
    PREPARE an empty mapping production_by_time.
    PREPARE an empty mapping attraction_by_time.
    PREPARE interval validity and discarded-record diagnostics.
    FOR EACH requested interval t:
        SUBMIT process_OD_array_of_each_timestamp(t) independently.
        Parallel execution may change scheduling, not output ordering.
    END FOR
    COLLECT interval results keyed by timestamp.
    SORT results by the declared time axis.
    REQUIRE every requested interval has a result or an explicit missing marker.
    FOR EACH valid interval result:
        STORE actual OD in actual_by_time[t].
        STORE the explicit singleton-column slice production[:,0] as production_by_time[t][N].
        STORE attraction[:,0] as attraction_by_time[t][N], preserving the identical station order.
        CHECK total production equals total attraction.
        CHECK both equal total resolved passenger multiplicity.
    END FOR
    BUILD intermediate_dic.T_N_D_ODs from actual_by_time.
    BUILD intermediate_dic.Trip_Production_In_Station_or_Out_Station from row totals.
    BUILD intermediate_dic.Trip_Attraction_In_Station_or_Out_Station from column totals.
    ADD station order, time axis, target definition, and split metadata.
    ADD observation-store reference if event-time construction is supported.
    ADD label completeness and unresolved-journey counts by entry cohort.

    ADD validation diagnostics without passenger identifiers.
    CALL save_to_pickle(intermediate_dic, result_array_file_path).
    RETURN intermediate_dic.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE generate_OD_DO_array.process_OD_array_of_each_timestamp
    INPUT time: one requested entry interval.
    CAPTURE grouped records and immutable station maps from outer procedure.
    OUTPUT time, od_matrix[N,N], production[N,1], attraction[N,1].
    INITIALIZE od_matrix with zero counts.
    SELECT records entering during time.
    IF the interval is missing rather than observed empty:
        RETURN the declared missing-interval status.
    END IF
    FOR EACH resolved record in this interval:
        MAP entry AFC code to origin m.
        MAP exit AFC code to destination n.
        CHECK both indices are valid.
        CHECK count is finite and nonnegative.
        CHECK exit_time is not earlier than entry_time when available.
        ADD count to od_matrix[m,n].
    END FOR
    FOR EACH canonical station m:
        production[m,0] <- SUM over n of od_matrix[m,n].
    END FOR
    FOR EACH canonical station n:
        attraction[n,0] <- SUM over m of od_matrix[m,n].
    END FOR
    CHECK the counted record population agrees with the declared label policy.

    RETURN time, od_matrix, production, attraction.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE save_to_pickle
    INPUT data: artifact payload with metadata.
    INPUT filename: intended local destination.
    OUTPUT write receipt or explicit failure.
    NOTE the legacy name denotes serialization, not a required executable format.
    VERIFY destination parent and write policy.
    VERIFY payload schema before serialization.
    WRITE to a temporary sibling artifact.
    FINISH and close the serialization stream.
    REOPEN the temporary artifact with the matching trusted reader.
    VERIFY shape, key set, and version metadata.
    PUBLISH the temporary artifact as the requested destination.
    IF any stage fails:
        CLOSE handles and retain an error diagnostic.
    END IF
    RETURN destination and payload summary.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE print_array_info
    INPUT array or structured artifact.
    OUTPUT human-readable diagnostic only.
    REPORT shape and axis names.
    REPORT data type and finite-value status.
    REPORT valid sample count and missing-sample count.
    IF numeric:
        REPORT minimum, maximum, and total where meaningful.
    END IF
    IF timestamp-indexed:
        REPORT first and last timestamp and ordering validity.
    END IF
    REPORT aggregate diagnostics only.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE generate_T_N_D_ODs
    INPUT result_array_all[T,N,N]: actual or finished raw matrices.
    INPUT top_D_stations: retained count R.
    INPUT mapping_artifact: already fitted RDS for all origins.
    OUTPUT result_array[T,N,R+1].
    REQUIRE 0 <= R < N for the residual-slot formulation.
    REQUIRE the mapping was fitted using training intervals only.
    REQUIRE mapping station order matches input station order.
    ALLOCATE result_array with the input count precision.
    FOR EACH origin m:
        retained <- mapping_artifact.RDS[m] in its stored order.
        remaining <- mapping_artifact.residual_set[m].
        CHECK retained contains R distinct valid destinations.
        CHECK retained and remaining partition all N destinations.
        INITIALIZE volume-coverage diagnostic accumulator.
        FOR EACH interval t:
            FOR retained slot k from 0 through R-1:
                result_array[t,m,k] <- result_array_all[t,m,retained[k]].
            END FOR
            result_array[t,m,R] <- SUM raw flow over remaining.
            CHECK compressed row total equals raw row total.
            IF raw row total is positive:
                RECORD explicitly retained volume divided by raw row total.
            ELSE:
                RECORD undefined volume share for that empty row.
            END IF
        END FOR
        REPORT valid volume-share diagnostics separately from dimension ratio.
    END FOR

    RETURN result_array and optional coverage diagnostics.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE fit_training_destination_mapping
    INPUT training_actual[T_train,N,N], retained count R, station order.
    OUTPUT mapping_artifact with RDS, residual sets, and residual weights.
    REQUIRE every fitting timestamp belongs to the training period.
    REQUIRE finite nonnegative counts and a declared completed-cohort fitting population.
    REJECT unknown/unresolved destination labels represented as zeros in the ranking corpus.
    FOR EACH origin m:
        cumulative[n] <- SUM training_actual[:,m,n].
        SORT destinations by descending cumulative flow.
        RESOLVE ties using a documented deterministic convention.
        RDS[m] <- first R destination identifiers.
        residual_set[m] <- all other destination identifiers.
        residual_total <- SUM cumulative[n] over residual_set[m].
        SET residual weights for retained destinations to zero.
        FOR EACH residual destination n:
            IF residual_total > 0:
                weight[m,n] <- cumulative[n] / residual_total.
            ELSE:
                weight[m,n] <- 1 / (N-R).
            END IF
        END FOR
        CHECK residual weights sum to one.
    END FOR
    RECORD fitting time range and mapping version.
    FREEZE the mapping for training, validation, and testing.
    RETURN mapping_artifact.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE time_in_interval
    INPUT t: timestamp with a declared service timezone.
    INPUT start, end: service-window clock boundaries.
    OUTPUT outside_service_window: Boolean.
    NOTE the retained legacy caller uses TRUE to reject a timestamp.
    EXTRACT the clock portion of t in the service timezone.
    IF start precedes end on the same day:
        ACCEPT clock times inside the declared non-wrapping interval.
    ELSE IF start follows end:
        ACCEPT clock times from start through midnight and midnight through end.
    ELSE:
        REQUIRE an explicit all-day or empty-window interpretation.
    END IF
    APPLY the configured inclusion rule at exact boundaries.
    RETURN NOT accepted.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE build_sample_plan(interval_grid, split_manifest, sample_policy, L_h, L_f)
    INPUT ordered interval starts, target split, service-window and boundary policy, independent lengths.
    OUTPUT plan: ordered records {sample_id, forecast_origin, input_times, target_times}.
    CHECK L_h > 0 and L_f > 0
    delta <- sample_policy.interval_duration
    plan <- empty list
    FOR EACH t0 in interval_grid:
        input_times <- [t0-L_h*delta, ..., t0-delta]
        target_times <- [t0, ..., t0+(L_f-1)*delta]
        IF any target time lies outside split_manifest:
            CONTINUE
        END IF
        IF any input or target time is excluded by sample_policy.service_window:
            CONTINUE
        END IF
        IF sample_policy forbids the resulting service-day crossing:
            CONTINUE
        END IF
        sample_id <- stable ID of dataset, split, t0, L_h, L_f and window-policy version
        APPEND {sample_id, forecast_origin=t0, input_times, target_times} to plan
    END FOR
    RETURN plan
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE generating_trip_generation_data_and_OD_dict
    INPUT top_D_stations=R, base_dir, prefix, str_prdc_attr, seq_len=L_h, horizon=L_f.
    INPUT everyday_start_time_str, everyday_end_time_str, interval duration and sample_policy.
    INPUT frozen mapping, observation_store, prefix interval labels and permitted history stores.
    INPUT auxiliary_required, generation_signal_bundle, history_required, optional sample_plan.
    OUTPUT {sample_artifact, feature_artifact_or_absent, manifest, diagnostics}.
    labels <- READ prefix_result_array
    mapping <- LOAD frozen training-derived destination mapping
    actual <- generate_T_N_D_ODs(labels.full_OD, R, mapping)
    IF L_f is absent:
        L_f <- sample_policy.explicit_legacy_horizon
    END IF
    CHECK L_h > 0 and L_f > 0
    IF sample_plan is absent:
        sample_plan <- build_sample_plan(labels.interval_grid, prefix split_manifest, sample_policy, L_h, L_f)
    ELSE:
        CHECK sample_plan dataset, split, lengths, interval and policy IDs match this request
    END IF

    feature_stores <- absent
    IF auxiliary_required:
        feature_stores <- LOAD production and attraction from generation_signal_bundle
        NORMALIZE prdc/attr task aliases to production/attraction
        IF a single-task compatibility adapter was explicitly selected:
            LABEL its output PARTIAL_TASK_BUNDLE and use its separate artifact destination
        END IF
        INDEX each task's covariates by full timestamp and availability time
    END IF
    samples <- empty list
    rejected <- empty list
    diagnostics <- empty aggregate report

    FOR EACH planned_sample in sample_plan:
        t0 <- planned_sample.forecast_origin
        sample_id <- planned_sample.sample_id
        input_times <- planned_sample.input_times
        target_times <- planned_sample.target_times
        buffer <- {sample_id, forecast_origin=t0, xtime=input_times, ytime=target_times}
        buffer.finished <- empty list
        buffer.unfinished_raw <- empty list
        buffer.y <- empty list
        buffer.target_observation_mask <- empty list
        sample_status <- ACCEPT
        IF auxiliary_required:
            buffer.historical_features <- empty task-keyed lists
            buffer.future_features <- empty task-keyed lists
        END IF
        IF history_required:
            buffer.history_day_raw <- empty list
            buffer.history_week_raw <- empty list
            buffer.history_month_raw <- empty list
            buffer.reference_metadata <- empty list
        END IF

        FOR EACH tau in planned_sample.input_times:
            observation <- build_cutoff_observations(tau, t0, observation_store)
            IF observation is unavailable:
                observation <- sample_policy.resolve_missing_input(tau, t0)
            END IF
            IF observation.status=REJECT:
                sample_status <- REJECT
                BREAK
            END IF
            finished <- generate_T_N_D_ODs(observation.finished_raw with a singleton time axis, R, mapping)[0]
            APPEND finished to buffer.finished
            APPEND observation.unfinished to buffer.unfinished_raw
            IF auxiliary_required:
                features <- SELECT each task's covariates at tau with available_at <= t0
                APPLY sample_policy.missing_covariate_rule to unavailable features
                APPEND features to buffer.historical_features by task
            END IF
        END FOR

        IF sample_status=ACCEPT:
            FOR EACH tau in planned_sample.target_times:
                target <- GET actual[tau] or MISSING
                completeness <- GET labels.completeness[tau] or UNKNOWN
                IF target is missing or completeness is insufficient:
                    resolution <- sample_policy.resolve_target(target, completeness)
                    IF resolution.status=REJECT:
                        sample_status <- REJECT
                        BREAK
                    END IF
                    (target, mask) <- resolution.target_and_valid_compressed_slot_mask
                    MASK every affected compressed origin row when an unresolved destination has no identifiable slot
                ELSE:
                    mask <- all true[N,R+1]
                END IF
                APPEND target to buffer.y
                APPEND mask to buffer.target_observation_mask
                IF auxiliary_required:
                    features <- SELECT target-time covariates announced or forecastable by t0
                    APPLY sample_policy.missing_covariate_rule to unavailable features
                    APPEND features and their availability provenance to buffer.future_features by task
                END IF
            END FOR
        END IF

        IF history_required AND sample_status=ACCEPT:
            FOR EACH source in {day, week, month}:
                FOR EACH tau in planned_sample.input_times:
                    reference_time <- MAP tau to the previous calendar day, seven days,
                                        or same calendar date in the previous month for source
                    reference_value <- UNAVAILABLE
                    metadata <- {source, requested_time=reference_time, status=missing}
                    IF reference_time exists:
                        record <- SELECT history record at reference_time available by t0
                        IF record has complete actual destinations:
                            reference_value <- generate_T_N_D_ODs(record.OD with a singleton time axis, R, mapping)[0]
                            metadata <- record timestamp, availability and observed status
                        END IF
                    END IF
                    IF reference_value=UNAVAILABLE:
                        resolution <- sample_policy.resolve_missing_history(source, reference_time, t0)
                        IF resolution.status=REJECT:
                            sample_status <- REJECT
                            BREAK
                        END IF
                        reference_value <- resolution.value_or_missing_marker
                        metadata <- resolution.provenance_and_status
                    END IF
                    APPEND reference_value to buffer["history_" + source + "_raw"]
                    APPEND metadata to buffer.reference_metadata
                END FOR
                IF sample_status=REJECT:
                    BREAK
                END IF
            END FOR
        END IF

        IF any required covariate rule rejected this buffer:
            sample_status <- REJECT
        END IF
        IF sample_status=REJECT:
            APPEND {sample_id=planned_sample.sample_id, reasons} to rejected
            CONTINUE
        END IF
        CHECK all active streams have the planned lengths and timestamps
        APPEND buffer to samples
    END FOR

    B <- length(samples)
    payload.finished <- STACK samples.finished as [B,L_h,N,R+1]
    payload.unfinished_raw <- STACK samples.unfinished_raw as [B,L_h,N,1]
    payload.y <- STACK samples.y as [B,L_f,N,R+1]
    payload.target_observation_mask <- STACK masks as [B,L_f,N,R+1]
    payload.xtime, payload.ytime <- STACK planned input and target timestamps
    payload.sample_id, payload.forecast_origin <- sample IDs and origins
    payload.RDS_id <- mapping.RDS_id
    manifest.aliases <- {sample_ids:sample_id, unfinished:unfinished_raw}
    manifest.units <- passenger_count
    manifest.optional_fields <- active fields for this component plan
    IF history_required:
        FOR EACH source in {day, week, month}:
            payload["history_" + source + "_raw"] <- STACK references as [B,L_h,N,R+1]
        END FOR
        manifest.history <- {representation_kind=reference_od, scale=passenger_count}
        manifest.reference_metadata <- per-sample source timestamps, availability and status
        ADD only caller-declared history_day/week/month and history_short/history_long aliases
    END IF
    feature_artifact <- absent
    IF auxiliary_required:
        feature_payload <- {historical_features, future_features, task_schemas, sample_id, xtime, ytime}
        IF both tasks share identical covariates:
            STORE one immutable feature payload with two task references
        END IF
        ADD explicit features/additional_feature compatibility aliases
        feature_artifact <- save_to_pickle(feature_payload, configured split feature destination)
    END IF
    payload.encoder_knowledge, payload.decoder_knowledge <- PENDING_JOIN_BY_SAMPLE_ID
    sample_artifact <- save_to_pickle(payload and manifest, configured split sample destination)
    FOR EACH numeric payload tensor:
        print_array_info(tensor)
    END FOR
    diagnostics.rejected <- rejected
    RETURN {sample_artifact, feature_artifact, manifest, diagnostics}
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE build_cutoff_observations(entry_interval, forecast_cutoff, observation_store)
    INPUT entry interval, observation cutoff and event-timed store with cohort/coverage policy.
    OUTPUT {status, finished_raw[N,N], unfinished[N,1], coverage, conservation_status}.
    CHECK entry_interval ends by forecast_cutoff
    coverage <- observation_store.entry_coverage(entry_interval, forecast_cutoff)
    IF coverage is insufficient for the configured censored-input policy:
        RETURN {status=REJECT, reason=incomplete_entry_coverage}
    END IF
    journeys <- SELECT eligible deduplicated entries in entry_interval observed by forecast_cutoff
    finished_raw <- zeros[N,N]
    unfinished <- zeros[N,1]
    FOR EACH journey in journeys:
        IF its exit occurred and was observed by forecast_cutoff:
            finished_raw[journey.origin, journey.observed_destination] += journey.count
        ELSE:
            unfinished[journey.origin,0] += journey.count
        END IF
    END FOR
    conservation_status <- CENSORED
    IF complete offline labels and complete entries are available for this same eligible cohort:
        CHECK row_sums(actual) = row_sums(finished_raw) + unfinished[:,0]
        conservation_status <- VERIFIED
    END IF
    RETURN {status=ACCEPT, finished_raw, unfinished, coverage, conservation_status}
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE process_data_D
    INPUT the legacy aggregation, split, task, and window arguments.
    INPUT the same mapping and temporal contracts as the main generator.
    OUTPUT a reduced OD sample artifact with explicit observability metadata.
    READ prefix_result_array and actual labels.
    LOAD the fixed RDS mapping.
    COMPRESS labels without changing destination ranks.
    BUILD the identical sample_manifest used by the full-data generator.
    FOR EACH forecast origin in that manifest:
        BUILD cutoff-visible finished inputs from event-timed records.
        RETAIN actual future matrices as targets only.
        RECORD input and target timestamp arrays.
    END FOR
    IF this reduced routine intentionally omits unfinished inputs:
        LABEL the result as an ablation-input artifact.
    END IF

    SAVE to a distinct artifact name or an explicitly selected alternative.

    RETURN reduced artifact and manifest.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE Connect_to_SQL
    INPUT prefix, train_sql, test_sql, val_sql.
    INPUT station_manager_dict_file_path and externally supplied connection settings.
    OUTPUT df, time_axis, station_to_codes, code_to_station.
    READ the canonical station dictionary.
    SELECT the configured read query matching prefix.
    REJECT unknown prefix rather than selecting an unrelated default month.
    REQUIRE an explicit column schema and declared date bounds.
    OPEN a database connection without printing connection secrets.
    TRY:
        OPEN a cursor.
        EXECUTE the authorized read query using bound date parameters.
        FETCH rows and column metadata.
        VERIFY actual returned columns match the declared schema.
        REQUIRE entry time and origin code for observable entries.
        REQUIRE exit time and destination code for resolved exits.
        ACCEPT legacy entry-cohort final counts only for actual-label construction.
        MATERIALIZE rows in a table with semantic names.
    ON database error:
        REPORT sanitized source and query-stage information.
        RETURN failure without partial dataset artifacts.
    FINALLY:
        CLOSE cursor if opened.
        CLOSE connection if opened.
    END TRY
    NORMALIZE station names using an explicit station-alias table.
    COLLECT all entry codes seen for each canonical station name.
    COLLECT all exit codes seen for each canonical station name.
    UNION both sets; do not prefer the exit set and discard entry aliases.
    MERGE the reviewed supplemental code table.
    LEGACY SUPPLEMENTAL MAPPING FOR REVIEW:
        新市桥 -> 521; 南门 -> 522; 南园北路 -> 523.
        竹辉桥 -> 524; 荷花荡 -> 525; 黄天荡 -> 526.
        金厍桥 -> 527; 星波街 -> 528; 李公堤南 -> 529.
        金湖 -> 530; 华莲 -> 531; 斜塘 -> 532.
        苏州奥体中心 -> 533; 方洲公园 -> 534; 星塘街 -> 535.
        龙墩 -> 536; 东沙湖 -> 537; 葑亭大道 -> 538.
        阳澄湖南 -> 539.
        双桥 and 红庄 legacy zero entries mean unresolved, not valid AFC code zero.
    REQUIRE this mapping to match the supplied data period before use.
    REMOVE duplicate aliases per canonical station.
    BUILD the inverse code_to_station map.
    IF any code maps to multiple distinct canonical stations:
        REPORT the conflict and require explicit reconciliation.
    END IF
    IF a network station has no observed code:
        RETAIN its canonical row with a missing-mapping status.
    END IF
    PARSE timestamps in the declared timezone and precision.
    CONSTRUCT the complete requested interval grid.
    DISTINGUISH known empty intervals from absent extracts.
    SORT the grid and verify uniqueness.
    RETURN reconciled rows, grid, forward map, inverse map.
END PROCEDURE
